<![CDATA[One Bit that sets device output in Auto or Manual]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="AutoEnable" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="ZZZZZZZZZZDevice50" BitNumber="3" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A bit to enable a device to run in Auto with other devices in Auto]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="HMI_AutoSelect" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="ZZZZZZZZZZDevice50" BitNumber="4" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Select auto mode for device]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="HMI_ManualSelect" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="ZZZZZZZZZZDevice50" BitNumber="5" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Select manual mode for device]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="AutoArmed" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="ZZZZZZZZZZDevice50" BitNumber="6" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Tells the system device is in auto,  but will needd fresh reestart to start when transitioning from manual back to Auto]]>
</Description>
</Member>
<Member Name="HMI_DeviceReset" DataType="BIT" Dimension="0" Radix="Decimal" Hidden="false" Target="ZZZZZZZZZZDevice50" BitNumber="7" ExternalAccess="Read/Write">
<Description>
<![CDATA[A bit that will be used to clear all interlocks and faultss specific to one device]]>
</Description>
</Member>
